SUMMARY:Tenants of Tender Armour - Exhibition series: April – December 2026
DESCRIPTION:Tenants of Tender Armour\nApril – December 2026\nACUD Galerie\n\n“The notion of the body is tied to the idea of the individual and conceived of as bounded and complete\, a productive and ableist entity to be fixed and saved.\nBut where is the place for\, and the recognition of bodies that do not correspond to this framework\; of bodies that do not have the possibility to access the protective resources deposited there?”*\n\nTenants of Tender Armour is a ten-month program (April–December 2026) that unfolds in three exhibition acts and accompanying events. It explores shielding as a material practice and a micropolitical gesture. Shielding manifests itself in the context of war and conflict\, where bodies function as literal shields\, but also in everyday life: in small movements and gestures that people use to protect themselves from visibility or to cope with structural violence. These embodied tactics translate large socio-political forces into intimate physical codes and movements. Our program takes this ambivalence as its starting point. Shielding is understood as a sonic and relational practice that creates permeable membranes of delicate protective spaces.\n\nParticipating artists:\nJosefin Arnell\, Jordan Deal\, Dina El Kaisy Friemuth\, Manuel Goetz\, Samuel Guerrero\, Kasra Jalilipour\, Julia Selin\, Joshua Tarelle Reid\, TABLOID Press\, Zhiyuan Yang\n… more to be announced\n\nAct I\n30.04–28.06.2026\nEcho Alliances\nCocurated with Carmen Herold\n\nAct II\n23.07–20.09.2026\nhttps://acudmachtneu.de/events/2357/a-charm-of-powerful-trouble/\n\nAct III\n01.10–06.12.2026\nOrbital Decay\n\n\nThe project is curated by:\nColette Patterson & Gabriela Matuszewska\n\nVisual identification: Charlotte Rohde\n\nIn collaboration with Goethe-Institut im Exil\n\nCurated by ACUD Galerie\n\nACUD Galerie is funded by the Basisförderung der Senatsverwaltung für Kultur und Gesellschaftlichen Zusammenhalt.\n\n*Noeth\, S.\, Umathum\, S.\, and Jansa\, J. (2024). Shielding. transcript Verlag.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Tenants of Tender Armour<br />\nApril – December 2026</strong><br />\nACUD Galerie</p>\n<p>“The notion of the body is tied to the idea of the individual and conceived of as bounded and complete\, a productive and ableist entity to be fixed and saved.<br />\nBut where is the place for\, and the recognition of bodies that do not correspond to this framework\; of bodies that do not have the possibility to access the protective resources deposited there?”*</p>\n<p><strong>Tenants of Tender Armour</strong> is a ten-month program (April–December 2026) that unfolds in three exhibition acts and accompanying events. It explores shielding as a material practice and a micropolitical gesture. Shielding manifests itself in the context of war and conflict\, where bodies function as literal shields\, but also in everyday life: in small movements and gestures that people use to protect themselves from visibility or to cope with structural violence. These embodied tactics translate large socio-political forces into intimate physical codes and movements. Our program takes this ambivalence as its starting point. Shielding is understood as a sonic and relational practice that creates permeable membranes of delicate protective spaces.</p>\n<p><strong>Participating artists:</strong><br />\nJosefin Arnell\, Jordan Deal\, Dina El Kaisy Friemuth\, Manuel Goetz\, Samuel Guerrero\, Kasra Jalilipour\, Julia Selin\, Joshua Tarelle Reid\, TABLOID Press\, Zhiyuan Yang<br />\n… more to be announced</p>\n<p><strong>Act I<br />\n30.04–28.06.2026<br />\n<a href=https://acudmachtneu.de/events/2332/echo-alliances/ rel=noopener target=_blank>Echo Alliances</a></strong><br />\nCocurated with Carmen Herold</p>\n<p><strong>Act II<br />\n23.07–20.09.2026</strong><br />\n<strong>https://acudmachtneu.de/events/2357/a-charm-of-powerful-trouble/</p>\n<p>Act III<br />\n01.10–06.12.2026<br />\n<a href=https://acudmachtneu.de/events/2379/orbital-decay/ rel=noopener target=_blank>Orbital Decay</a></strong></p>\n<p>The project is curated by:<br />\nColette Patterson &#038\; Gabriela Matuszewska</p>\n<p>Visual identification: Charlotte Rohde</p>\n<p>In collaboration with Goethe-Institut im Exil</p>\n<p>Curated by ACUD Galerie</p>\n<p>ACUD Galerie is funded by the Basisförderung der Senatsverwaltung für Kultur und Gesellschaftlichen Zusammenhalt.</p>\n<p>*Noeth\, S.\, Umathum\, S.\, and Jansa\, J. (2024). Shielding. transcript Verlag.</p>\n
